      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T22:05:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `api_surface` should be a property of java_api_provider and not java_api_library. As a hypothetical example,\n```\n$ ls\nAndroid.bp\ncurrent.txt\nsystem-current.txt\n\n$ cat Android.bp\njava_api_provider {\n  name: \"my_public_contribution\",\n  api_file: \"current.txt\",\n}\njava_api_provider {\n  name: \"my_system_contribution\",\n  api_file: \"system-current.txt\",\n}\n```\n\nWithout this attribute, the rdeps cannot differentiate if the APIs are coming from the publicapi component or the systemapi component. This differentiation might be helpful in the future to enforce various build rules.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1832,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1832,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "2d0d1b3e6506c63c6fef66a262cc8a91626ab35a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24394291_6e65a764",
        "filename": "java/java_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1832,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T00:41:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the naming of the final artifact `*-android.jar` prefixes the api surface, I believe this prop is essential to `java_api_library`. If the `api_surface` prop is specified in the provider rather than the rdep, it would need complicated rule to determine which api surface\u0027s jar it is generating. For instance, a rdep of the above hypothetical example may look like this:\n```\njava_api_library {\n  name: \"my_api_surface\",\n  // api_surface: \"system\",\n  api_providers: [\n    \"my_public_contribution\",\n    \"my_system_contribution\"\n  ],\n}\n\n```\nWithout the `api_surface` param, how can the module determine that the name of the final artifact should be `system-android.jar`? (because complete system api surface is contributed by both public api domains and system api domains, and similarly for test api surface) \n\nRegarding your concern about component distinguishability, I believe it is somewhat self-explanatory from the prefixes of the `*{-}current.txt` api files. If you believe if would be more beneficial when explicit, I will add the prop to `java_api_provider`",
      "parentUuid": "94eb1516_6c5c46ad",
